 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How a literary text is built",
     "texto": [
      "A story doesn't inform: it **makes you see and feel**. In Vietnamese it achieves this mainly with three resources:",
      "**So sánh** (comparison) with **như**, **như là**, **tựa như**, **chẳng khác gì**: «mưa rơi **như** ai đang gõ cửa» = the rain falls as if someone were knocking at the door.",
      "**Nhân hóa** (personification): things do what people do: «cái bếp **thở** ra khói», «con phố **ngủ**», «gió **thì thầm**».",
      "**Từ láy** (repeated words), which here do not soften: they **paint a sound or an image**: **rì rào** (the rumble of wind or water), **lách tách** (drops, crackling), **thì thầm** (whispering), **lặng lẽ** (silently), **thoang thoảng** (a faint smell), **chập chờn** (flickering, coming and going).",
      "Also, the literary sentence **stretches or cuts short** on purpose, and often **drops the subject**. Don't try to translate word for word: read the whole sentence and ask yourself what image it leaves."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
